ource_name": "Simon Willison's Weblog", "source_native_id": "https://simonwillison.net/2026/Oct/22/de-staat-freedom/", "source_policy": "public_official", "source_type": "primary_artifact", "summary_hint": "<p><strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hKO4pQtIXow\">DE STAAT - FREEDOM (Official Music Video)</a></strong></p>\nOK well this is a first for me... at <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hKO4pQtIXow&amp;t=44s\">00:44</a> in this new music video by Dutch alternative rock band <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/De_Staat\">De Staat</a>:</p>\n<p><video\n  src=\"https://static.simonwillison.net/static/2026/freedom-pelican.mp4\"\n  poster=\"https://static.simonwillison.net/static/2026/freedom-pelican-poster.jpg\"\n  preload=\"none\"\n  loop=\"1\" controls=\"1\"\n  playsinline=\"1\" muted=\"1\"\n  width=\"1280\"\n  height=\"720\"\n  style=\"display: block; width: 100%; height: auto;\"\n> </video>\n</p>\n<p>The visual effects are credited to Matties Grooten of <a href=\"https://fakeitorleaveit.com\">Fake it or Leave it</a>.\n\n    <p><small></small>Via <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50186129#50193407\">flir on Hacker News</a></small></p>\n\n\n    <p>Tags: <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/music\">music</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/ai\">ai</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/generative-ai\">generative-ai</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/pelican-riding-a-bicyc", "title": "DE STAAT - FREEDOM (Official Music Video)", "topics": ["topic_staat-freedom-official-music-video"], "updated_at": null}
{"artifact_links": ["https://simonwillison.net/2026/Oct/22/donating-agent-skills"], "author_or_org": null, "canonical_url": "https://simonwillison.net/2026/Oct/22/donating-agent-skills", "collection_method": "rss_atom", "confidence": "high", "content_hash": "2d16bbb0a880f965", "dedup_key": "rss-guid:simonwillison-blog:https://simonwillison.net/2026/Oct/22/donating-agent-skills/", "event_id": "event_ba20ea2eb0544c22", "evidence_type": "supported_fact", "excerpt": "<p><strong><a href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/donating-agent-skills-to-the-agentic-ai-foundation\">Donating Agent Skills to the Agentic AI Foundation</a></strong></p>\nNews today from Anthropic:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>We\u2019re committed to keeping Agent Skills open, community-driven, and vendor-neutral. Today, we are donating the standard to the Agentic AI Foundation (AAIF) under the Linux Foundation, <a href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/donating-the-model-context-protocol-and-establishing-of-the-agentic-ai-foundation\">which we co-founded</a> with Block and OpenAI last year, and to which we donated the Model Context Protocol (MCP).</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I'm pleased to note I called this one <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2025/Dec/19/agent-skills/\">last December</a>, when Anthropic first declared skills to be an \"open standard\":</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I wouldn't be surprised to see this end up <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2025/Dec/9/agentic-ai-foundation/\">in the AAIF</a>, recently the new home of the MCP specification.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Fun side note: since my blog content is available to Claude via the <a href=\"https://github.com/datasette/datasette-mcp\">datasette-mcp</a>", "identifiers": {}, "inferred_entities": [], "item_type": "rss_atom_item", "novelty_score": 0.0, "published_at": "2026-10-22T18:09:56+00:00", "ranking_explanation": "", "raw_metadata": {}, "relevance_score": 0.0, "retrieved_at": "2026-10-22T22:10:11Z", "source_id": "simonwillison-blog", "source_name": "Simon Willison's Weblog", "source_native_id": "https://simonwillison.net/2026/Oct/22/donating-agent-skills/", "source_policy": "public_official", "source_type": "primary_artifact", "summary_hint": "<p><strong><a href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/donating-agent-skills-to-the-agentic-ai-foundation\">Donating Agent Skills to the Agentic AI Foundation</a></strong></p>\nNews today from Anthropic:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>We\u2019re committed to keeping Agent Skills open, community-driven, and vendor-neutral. Today, we are donating the standard to the Agentic AI Foundation (AAIF) under the Linux Foundation, <a href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/donating-the-model-context-protocol-and-establishing-of-the-agentic-ai-foundation\">which we co-founded</a> with Block and OpenAI last year, and to which we donated the Model Context Protocol (MCP).</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I'm pleased to note I called this one <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2025/Dec/19/agent-skills/\">last December</a>, when Anthropic first declared skills to be an \"open standard\":</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I wouldn't be surprised to see this end up <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2025/Dec/9/agentic-ai-foundation/\">in the AAIF</a>, recently the new home of the MCP specification.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Fun side note: since my blog content is available to Claude via the <a href=\"https://github.com/datasette/datasette-mcp\">datasette-mcp</a>", "title": "Donating Agent Skills to the Agentic AI Foundation", "topics": ["topic_donating-agent-skills-the-agentic"], "updated_at": null}
